{
  "schema": "fx-data/v1",
  "_doc": "Monkey Bananas runtime FX. Owner: Technical Artist. Consumer: Game Developer (texture-baker.ts createFxPlayer, or your own loader via resolveEmitter). Shape follows gamestudio particle-and-fx-authoring/references/fx-data-schema.md, with these project extensions: 'count' is the burst size passed to emitter.explode(count, x, y); 'bindings' map config fields (or 'count') to feel-tunable keys in src/core/tuning.ts, so tuning.ts stays the single source of truth and the numbers written here are fallbacks equal to today's tunables; 'spread' turns a bound scalar into a {min,max} of +/- that fraction; 'arc' builds the angle range (Phaser angles: 0 = right, 90 = down, 270 = straight up); 'tintChars' are PALETTE chars resolved at runtime (exact palette colours, no hex duplicated here); 'pixelSnap' is the render grid in logical px (= the particle's integer scale, README per-sprite snap rule); 'reducedMotion' may only disable an emitter or scale its count (countFactor = number or a tuning key). Every emitter: texture mb_atlas, blend NORMAL (no ADD: it would break the batch and push colours off-palette), constant integer scale (no scale-over-life: no fractional pixel art), no rotation (rotated pixel art crawls), fade by alpha only. Emitters live at (0,0) and burst at world coordinates. 'events' are cross-references only (fireFromFx false): the gameplay event wiring in motion/event-markers.md already fires the cue and the shake, so the FX player never double-fires them.",
  "atlas": "mb_atlas",
  "budget": {
    "targetDevice": "min-spec mobile (2019 mid-range Android, Mali-G52 class), 60 fps",
    "perFxPeakParticlesCap": 200,
    "perEmitterMaxAliveCap": 100,
    "gameplayMaxAliveTotal": 160,
    "gameplayMaxAliveTotal_note": "Sum of maxAliveParticles over every gameplay emitter (tap 40 + critChips 32 + critSparks 16 + goldChips 16 + goldSparks 8 + confetti 36 + dust 12 = 160). evolvePoof is a flipbook (<= 24 sprites) and runs under the evolve input lock.",
    "fillratePerFxCapMpx": 1.0,
    "sceneFxFillrateCapMpxPerFrame": 4.0,
    "drawCalls": "0 extra: every emitter uses mb_atlas + NORMAL blend + the default quad batch, so particles join the same batch as the sprites and text around them",
    "worstCaseSustained": "16 taps/s with Lucky Peel (10% crit) and a golden catch: about 17 tap chips + 7 crit chips + 3 crit sparks + 24 golden = 51 alive, 0.006 Mpx/frame",
    "odSevev_note": "od-sevev adds ballotConfetti 24 (ceremony input lock, runs alone) + dustPuff 8 + inkSpecks 12 = 44 alive at most, inside the 160-sprite pool. The coin-burst (motion-spec coin-burst: a 16 fps spin per coin) is NOT a particle emitter, because the player gives each particle one static frame: it runs as the engine's pooled per-coin tween with its own cap of 36 alive (animator budget), 36 Sprite2D, one texture per spin frame (prop_coin0-3). Everything uses flat NORMAL-blend sprites; no ADD blend anywhere."
  },
